/-
The stopped score martingale of `pr:inner` / `lem:M lower tail`
(`paper/idla-cylinder-gff.tex:1189`, `tex:1194-1197`).

`Support/PrInnerSupport.lean` defines the paper's score
`stoppedScore B h ζ t = ∑_{s<t} ( H_ζ(X̄_s, Ȳ_s) − 1/N )`, where
`H_ζ = hitProb B ζ` and `(X̄_s, Ȳ_s) = stoppedSettleSite B h · s`, and reduces
`lem:M lower tail` to the martingale property of `stoppedScore` (its hypothesis
`hmart`) plus the predictable-variation bound.  This file isolates the
martingale property.

The general statistic is `stoppedScoreOf B h H t = ∑_{s<t} H(X̄_s, Ȳ_s)`; the
paper's score is the case `H = fun p => hitProb B ζ p − 1/N`
(`stoppedScore_eq_stoppedScoreOf`, definitional).

## What is proved and what is isolated

The *algebraic* half is proved: given the one-step conditional-mean identity
`hcond : E[ H(X̄_k, Ȳ_k) | 𝓕_k ] =ᵐ 0` and adaptedness/integrability, the statistic
is a martingale (`martingale_of_condExp_sub_eq_zero_nat`).  This is the stopped
analogue of `harmonicMartingale_isMartingale`'s algebraic half
(`Support/MartingaleProperty.lean`).

Two inputs remain isolated, and neither is currently discharged by the library:

* `hadapted` — `StronglyAdapted (idlaFiltration B) (stoppedScoreOf B h H)`.
  `idlaFiltration B t = σ(settleSite B · j : j < t)` is generated by the *actual*
  settling sites, whereas `stoppedSettleSite B h · s` is a function of the walks
  `ω 0, …, ω s`.  Since `exitSite'` is not injective, `ω j` is not `𝓕`-measurable,
  so the stopped settle site is not obviously `𝓕_t`-measurable either.  The
  paper uses the filtration of the *stopped* process; a canonical
  `stoppedFiltration` generated by `stoppedSettleSite B h · j` is the natural
  carrier and does not exist yet.
* `hcond` — the stopped conditional-mean identity (`tex:1198-1206`).  It needs the
  conditional law of `stoppedSettleSite B h · k` given the past, i.e. the stopped
  analogue of `condExp_settleSite_eq_integral` together with
  `integral_exitSite_uniform_eq_zero_of_expDecayBelow` at the random set
  `stoppedCluster B h ω k ∩ R B (h-1)`.  `Support/HarmonicStoppedMass.lean`
  supplies the deterministic stopped-mass bookkeeping for that step.

Everything is on the canonical carrier; no `Driver`/`driverLaw`/`cluster`.
-/
import IdlaCyl.Support.PrInnerSupport
import IdlaCyl.Support.Stopped
import IdlaCyl.Support.HarmonicStoppedMass
import Mathlib.Probability.Martingale.Basic
import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.ConditionalExpectation.Basic

namespace IdlaCyl

open MeasureTheory Filter
open scoped BigOperators

variable (B : Base)

/-- The general stopped score `∑_{s<t} H(X̄_s, Ȳ_s)`, built from the exit
locations `stoppedSettleSite B h · s` of the stopped process `Ā_h`. -/
noncomputable def stoppedScoreOf (h : ℤ) (H : Site B → ℝ) (t : ℕ) (ω : TrajSeq B) : ℝ :=
  ∑ s ∈ Finset.range t, H (stoppedSettleSite B h ω s)

/-- The paper's `stoppedScore` is `stoppedScoreOf` for the centered kernel
`H = hitProb B ζ − 1/N` (`tex:1189`). -/
theorem stoppedScore_eq_stoppedScoreOf (h : ℤ) (ζ : Site B) (t : ℕ) (ω : TrajSeq B) :
    stoppedScore B h ζ t ω
      = stoppedScoreOf B h (fun p => hitProb B ζ p - 1 / (B.card : ℝ)) t ω := rfl

/-- **The algebraic half of the stopped score martingale.**  Given the one-step
conditional-mean identity `hcond` and the adaptedness/integrability of the
statistic, `stoppedScoreOf` is a martingale.  This is the stopped analogue of
`harmonicMartingale_isMartingale`'s algebraic half, by
`martingale_of_condExp_sub_eq_zero_nat`. -/
theorem stoppedScoreOf_isMartingale (h : ℤ) (H : Site B → ℝ)
    (hadapted : StronglyAdapted (idlaFiltration B)
      (fun t ω => stoppedScoreOf B h H t ω))
    (hcond : ∀ k, (idlaMeasure B)[fun ω : TrajSeq B => H (stoppedSettleSite B h ω k)
        | idlaFiltration B k] =ᵐ[idlaMeasure B] 0)
    (hint : ∀ t, Integrable (fun ω : TrajSeq B => stoppedScoreOf B h H t ω)
      (idlaMeasure B)) :
    Martingale (fun t ω => stoppedScoreOf B h H t ω) (idlaFiltration B) (idlaMeasure B) := by
  classical
  refine martingale_of_condExp_sub_eq_zero_nat hadapted hint ?_
  intro i
  have hstep : (fun ω : TrajSeq B => stoppedScoreOf B h H (i + 1) ω)
        - (fun ω : TrajSeq B => stoppedScoreOf B h H i ω)
      = fun ω : TrajSeq B => H (stoppedSettleSite B h ω i) := by
    funext ω
    simp only [Pi.sub_apply, stoppedScoreOf]
    rw [Finset.sum_range_succ]
    ring
  rw [hstep]
  exact hcond i

end IdlaCyl
